change:
  id: CHG-030
  title: Live proposals carry the full replacement file, and only realisable scopes are offered
  status: proposed
  intent: Make a live model's proposal mean what the realiser does with it. The realiser writes the proposal's text as the whole workflow file, but the prompt asks for "patch text", so a real model returns a unified diff and the candidate's workflow file becomes diff text. Found by the first live generation against a real provider on 2026-11-07.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - ADR-0002
    - ADR-0006
    - PAT-004

deltas:
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: A live proposal's text is the complete new content of the workflow file. The prompt says so in those words, and a proposal whose text is shaped like a unified diff is rejected by deterministic validation before any candidate is created.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: a live proposer returns the complete new workflow file
        then: the candidate's workflow file equals that text exactly and its checks run against it
      - id: S2
        when: a live proposer returns unified-diff-shaped text, such as lines beginning "--- ", "+++ " and "@@"
        then: validation fails naming diff-shaped content, no candidate worktree or branch is created, and the workflow file is never written with diff text
        and:
          - evidence - run nw1 promoted two candidates whose workflow.txt was literally "--- ...\n+++ ...\n@@\n publish-policy: allow\n-draft-check: skip\n+draft-check: run\n", because the fixture check only rejects an exact "draft-check: skip" line
          - the rule is deterministic text inspection; it does not ask a model whether the text is a diff
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: The scopes a live prompt offers are exactly the scopes the run's validator accepts, taken from one source in the runner wiring, for every live proposer - the openai-compatible and acp profiles alike - through a port default that a proposer which does not prompt for scope ignores.
    scenarios:
      - id: S3
        when: a live proposer is asked for a mutation
        then: the prompt's allowed scopes list only the scopes the run will realise (today WORKFLOW_DEFINITION), so the model is not invited to choose a scope the run will reject
        and:
          - review (GLM-5.3) found the first round restricted only the LangChain4j adapter, through an instanceof in EvolveRunner, so the acp profile still offered every scope
        and:
          - evidence - 2 of 6 live asks across runs nw1 and nw2 chose PROMPT or TOOL_CONFIGURATION, which the prompt offered and the validator rejects

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: cli/EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.aLiveProposalIsTheFullReplacementFile
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: cli/EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.aLiveProposalShapedLikeADiffIsRejectedBeforeAnyCandidateExists
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/WholeFileContentValidatorTest
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: adapters/LangChain4jMutationProposalAdapterTest.offersOnlyTheScopesItIsGiven
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: Acceptance tests S1 and S2 with a real-shaped (diff) stub response, seen red first
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: Deterministic whole-file validator, composed into the runner's validator chain
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: Prompt wording - "content - the complete new workflow file, not a diff"; field name kept as patch on the wire for compatibility, documented
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: One source of realisable scopes in EvolveRunner, passed to both validator and proposer
    status: completed
  - id: T5
    slice: README, ADR-0002 and ADR-0006 (both copies) record that the first live measurement was invalidated by this defect
    status: pending

non_goals:
  - applying unified diffs (rejected as more surface for no current gain)
  - realising PROMPT or TOOL_CONFIGURATION scopes
  - recording tokens for rejected attempts (CHG-031)
  - a journal entry and the raw model text for a proposal rejected on a single-candidate run; the console error line is the only trace today (review, Claude Sonnet). Recorded as a follow-up, not done here

risks:
  - Text inspection can reject a legitimate workflow file that happens to contain diff-like lines. Accepted for the toy-scale targets in use; the rule requires the leading "--- "/"+++ " header pair or an "@@" hunk line, not any line starting with + or -.
  - The validator is text inspection over known diff shapes (unified, indented unified, git header, context format). A diff in a shape it does not know, such as one with every line quoted, would still be written as the file; the prompt wording is the first defence and the toy check the last.
